 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. On the standard variable rate, investors pay more than owner-occupiers, and the gap is 0.58 percentage points.\n\nIn September 2026, the latest month available, the advertised standard variable rates were:\n- **Investors:** 9.35%\n- **Owner-occupiers:** 8.77%\n\nThe gap was the same in every month I checked, from January 2025 to September 2026. For example, in January 2025 investors paid 9.35% and owner-occupiers 8.77%. By August 2025 both had dropped, to 8.60% and 8.02%. Both rates then rose again from February 2026 and have been flat since May 2026.\n\nThese are the advertised indicator rates from the RBA's F5 table. Rates actually paid on new loans are lower, because most borrowers get discounts. Discounted rates may show a different gap. I can check the discounted rates or the RBA's F6 data on rates actually paid if you'd like.",
